WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:02.127
Hi everyone, we are very excited

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.462
to bring you a whole new
season of "Fate and Fabled."

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:06.297
Hang tight to the end
of this episode

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.049
where we'll be
revealing a fun surprise

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.051
for the upcoming
season, stay tuned.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:14.222
Gather round, ye nerds and
weirdos, to hear this epic tale

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:16.099
of a godly war where
each side goes,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.059
"I think we just might fail."

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:20.061
(host 2)
In old Norse lore,
a witch was burned,

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.313
not once, nor twice, but thrice.

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:24.232
On her behalf,
the war tide turned

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:26.317
and each side paid the price.

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:29.738
Cue years of war before
a fragile peace could be agreed,

00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:33.283
till one side's anger was
unleashed, misunderstood indeed.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.909
But wisdom won, did Odin roar,

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:36.703
"Hey, spit in this cup here,"

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:38.288
and thus added the vicious war

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.873
between the Aesir and the Vanir.

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:41.750
[mystical music]

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:46.421
How do you end a war
between gods?

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.256
With spit, of course.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:50.258
In Norse mythology,
two competing groups

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.593
of gods called the Aesir

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:54.095
and the Vanir fought
a devastating war

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.972
until they combined their saliva

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.266
to cement a remarkably
unique truce.

00:00:58.349 --> 00:00:59.726
Divine wars aren't rare.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.436
They can be found in
most mythologies

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:02.896
from around the world.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.440
The Greek Olympians fought
and defeated the Titans.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:08.234
The Hindu Devas were able
to banish the demonic Asuras

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:10.111
to something that
resembled hell.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.572
And Christian angels cast
the rebellious demons down

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:14.324
into actual hell.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.077
These conflicts usually end
with good triumphant over evil,

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.121
a reminder to us
mortals of what happens

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.248
when you stray from
the righteous path.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:24.793
But the war between the Aesir
and Vanir is different

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:27.420
because it doesn't
impose a moral hierarchy.

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.380
Instead, the two groups combined

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:32.175
into a single united pantheon.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.761
Maybe the Norse just like
some different story tropes,

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:36.387
but some scholars
think this myth

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:39.682
can provide insight into the
actual history of Scandinavia.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.267
How about we tell you the story

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.853
and then you can decide
for yourself what it means?

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.688
To understand
the Aesir and Vanir,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.856
let's take a closer look

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.942
at how Norse mythology
is structured.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:50.610
The universe, according
to Norse mythology,

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.737
is split up into nine
different worlds,

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.364
resting in the roots
and branches

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.407
of the Great Tree Yggdrasil.

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.326
Each world is inhabited
by a different race,

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.036
like the giants on Jotunheim

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.371
and the dwarves on Svartalfheim

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.748
and the wee blue folk
of Smurfheim.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:05.416
Okay, I made that last one up.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.252
But we humans lived on Midgard

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:10.088
and worshiped two
other races as gods,

00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:13.049
the Vanir of Vanaheim
and the Aesir of Asgard.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.843
The Vanir used their powerful
magic to help humans prosper

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:18.388
in agriculture,
wealth, and fertility.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.139
They were wise, thoughtful,

00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:22.809
and wielded a coveted
magic called Seidr,

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:25.770
which could foresee
and shape the future.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:27.772
The Aesir, on the other hand,
were more interested

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:31.109
in violence and war than
their magical counterparts.

00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:33.111
For them,
brute strength, bravery,

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:36.114
and loyalty were valued
above most other traits.

00:02:36.197 --> 00:02:37.365
[soft music]

00:02:37.448 --> 00:02:38.908
Hail, nerd, whatcha doing?

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.494
I'm gardening,
meathead, I'm a Vanir.

00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:43.329
I inspire the humans on Midgard

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:45.373
to grow crops and
gain more wealth.

00:02:45.456 --> 00:02:47.083
Well, I am an Aesir

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:50.211
and I incite the humans
towards violence and war.

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:52.422
Weird flex. I'm pretty sure
I'm gonna get more respect

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.715
for what I do.

00:02:53.798 --> 00:02:55.550
You would think that,
wouldn't you?

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.845
Most sources say the war started

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:01.973
as retaliation for an Aesir
act of cowardly violence.

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:05.143
One section from "The Poetic
Edda" tells us about Gullveig,

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:07.353
a witch goddess who
traveled to Asgard

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.731
and shared her magic
with the Aesir.

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:12.150
She gave the Aesir gifts,
granted their wishes

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:15.403
and brought prosperity to
the All Father Odin's Hall,

00:03:15.486 --> 00:03:17.488
for which the Aesir
were totally grateful.

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:18.865
I'm just kidding.

00:03:18.948 --> 00:03:21.826
These are the gods of violence
and war we're talking about.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.787
They feared that Gullveig's
generosity was making them soft

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.998
and complacent or gold drunk,

00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:29.208
which is one
translation of her name.

00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:31.544
So they decided to kill her,
first with spears,

00:03:31.628 --> 00:03:32.837
and when that didn't work

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:35.256
they burned her at
the stake three times

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.258
and three times she was reborn

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:39.469
from the ashes
thanks to her magic.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.263
They renamed her Heidr,
meaning Bright One.

00:03:42.347 --> 00:03:45.183
The texts don't specify where
this powerful woman came from

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:46.601
or what she wanted.

00:03:46.684 --> 00:03:48.394
One possible theory
is that Gullveig

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:50.855
was a Vanir goddess
Freya in disguise.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:52.815
This is just one moment in
the story where it splits

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:56.486
into multiple versions, just
like Marvel's many multiverses.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.696
(host 1)
Obviously, the Vanir
couldn't let this treatment

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.531
of one of their
own go unpunished.

00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:03.409
So they uncharacteristically
readied for war,

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:06.037
but the Aesir were always
prepared for battle.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.331
So when Odin learned
about the Vanir's plans

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.791
he was able to strike first.

00:04:11.125 --> 00:04:12.585
The two groups met
on the plain of war,

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:15.171
the same field where the
final battle in Ragnarok

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.131
was predestined to take place,

00:04:17.215 --> 00:04:20.176
and Odin threw the first
spear into enemy lines.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.970
The Eddas and other
remaining records

00:04:22.053 --> 00:04:25.014
of Norse lore don't provide
many details about the war

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.976
but imply that it was
devastating for both sides.

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:30.395
After the first battle,
the Vanir used their magic

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:33.898
to decimate the protective
walls that encircled Asgard.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:36.776
And later, when the gods hire
a giant to rebuild the wall,

00:04:36.859 --> 00:04:38.903
Loki will shapeshift
into a lady horse

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.947
and distract
the giant's stallion

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.949
so he can't finish
the job on time

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:46.035
and won't have to be paid
Freya's hand in marriage.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.912
Known as
the "Bugs Bunny Gambit,"

00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:51.082
it seems like a risky way
to get out of paying a bill.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:54.961
In return, the Aesir absolutely
wrecked the Vanir homestead

00:04:55.044 --> 00:04:57.422
with the battle prowess
that inspired centuries

00:04:57.505 --> 00:04:58.506
of Viking raids.

00:04:58.589 --> 00:05:00.883
War waged for years with magic

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.761
and physical strength taking
turns on the upper hand,

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:07.140
potions bested axes,
swords sliced through spells.

00:05:07.223 --> 00:05:09.976
Eventually the two sides
realized they were at an impasse

00:05:10.059 --> 00:05:11.602
and met to call a ceasefire.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.147
-Well, that was fun.
-Was it?

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.691
Yeah, I mean, maybe
we should join forces.

00:05:16.774 --> 00:05:18.609
With my bravery and strength
and your magic,

00:05:18.693 --> 00:05:20.528
we could be like
the best pantheon ever.

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:22.363
Like the Justice League meets--

00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:25.324
-The Avengers.
-I was gonna say Care Bears.

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:27.326
Oh yeah, that's fair.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.246
(host 2)
In the longstanding Germanic
and Scandinavian tradition,

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:32.498
each side cemented
the truce by sending some

00:05:32.582 --> 00:05:34.917
of their own to live
with their former foes.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.128
The Vanir sent Freya,
her brother Freyr,

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:39.881
and their father Njord
to live among the Aesir,

00:05:39.964 --> 00:05:42.884
while Hoenir and Mimir were
sent to live on Vanaheim.

00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:45.136
The three Vanirs settled
well into life on Asgard.

00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:47.847
But Hoenir and Mimir
weren't so fortunate.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:51.225
At first, the Vanir were so
enchanted by Hoenir's good looks

00:05:51.309 --> 00:05:53.895
and wisdom that they
made him their leader.

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:55.897
But when they found out
that Hoenir was just a dope

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.774
who was getting his
advice advice from Mimir,

00:05:57.857 --> 00:06:00.276
they were so mad that
they cut off Mimir's head

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.028
and sent it to Daddy Odin.

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:04.363
Odin used the seidr magic
that Vanir taught him

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:05.656
to keep meme's head alive

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.035
and thankfully avoided
another all-out war.

00:06:09.118 --> 00:06:10.578
The decapitation was written off

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:12.747
as nothing more than
a misunderstanding.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.499
I mean, who among us
hasn't gotten confused

00:06:14.582 --> 00:06:16.542
and lopped off
a former enemy's head?

00:06:16.626 --> 00:06:19.170
The Aesir and Vanir gathered
once more and debated,

00:06:19.253 --> 00:06:21.255
according to the "Voluspa" poem,

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:22.965
"Whether the gods
should tribute give

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.343
or to all alike
should worship belong?"

00:06:25.426 --> 00:06:27.303
The Vanir wanted
either compensation

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:29.055
for the way Gullveig
had been treated

00:06:29.138 --> 00:06:30.848
or equal worship by the humans.

00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:33.184
No more of this
"also featuring" bull.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.770
The Aesir agreed to
share their divine status

00:06:35.853 --> 00:06:37.396
and the two groups
secured their peace

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.981
by spitting into a cauldron.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.234
From the spit emerged
the god Kvasir,

00:06:41.317 --> 00:06:42.902
the wisest of all beings

00:06:42.985 --> 00:06:46.072
whose blood became the
legendary mead of poetry.

00:06:46.155 --> 00:06:47.657
We don't know why spit was used

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.493
to seal such a momentous
decision, but I love

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.538
that the practice lives on
in the modern spit shake.

00:06:53.621 --> 00:06:54.831
To the Aesir and Vanir!
[inhales]

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:59.001
Wait, why not to
the Vanir and Aesir?

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:01.796
It's alphabetical.

00:07:01.879 --> 00:07:02.880
Oh.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.175
So why is the ending
to this war so unique?

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:09.345
It's possible this story
and its spitty conclusion

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:11.514
where merely adopted and adapted

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.600
from proto Indo-European
cultures as they intermingled.

00:07:14.684 --> 00:07:16.686
But I'm personally
not convinced.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.063
The story's ending is
too unlike other myths

00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:20.565
from the region.

00:07:20.648 --> 00:07:23.776
Instead, I agree with
historians like Dr. John Lindow,

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.320
that this myth acts as
a blurred reflection

00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:28.072
of real world events.

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:30.575
We've talked about this
phenomenon on the show before.

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:33.619
An influential person or local
hero might be exaggerated

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:36.455
into a god like the
Yoruba King Shango,

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:38.374
who was deified as an Orisha

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.585
or a clash of cultures
could be remembered

00:07:40.668 --> 00:07:43.963
as a legendary war, much like
the six invasions described

00:07:44.046 --> 00:07:46.048
in the Irish
"Mythological Cycle."

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:49.343
Here, the hypothesis is that
Germanic tribes migrated north

00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:51.053
about 3,000 years ago,

00:07:51.137 --> 00:07:53.055
encountered
indigenous Scandinavians

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.891
with their own
differing pantheon

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:57.310
and incorporated it
into their own.

00:07:57.393 --> 00:07:58.936
We know that ancient
Germanic tribes

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.022
worshiped a war god named Wodin.

00:08:01.105 --> 00:08:03.608
And Roman records tell us that
they were skilled fighters

00:08:03.691 --> 00:08:05.109
so it's easy to imagine them

00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:07.653
following the war
hungry Aesir gods,

00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:10.031
but not the seidr
wielding Vanir.

00:08:10.114 --> 00:08:12.491
It seems much more likely
that the Vanir were worshiped

00:08:12.575 --> 00:08:14.702
by indigenous Scandinavians
who placed more

00:08:14.785 --> 00:08:17.914
of a societal emphasis on
connecting to the land.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:21.083
The Sami people, native to what
is now Northern Scandinavia,

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.586
had a shamanic religion
before they were Christianized

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:26.589
in the 16th century, and
their shamanic practices

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:29.217
might have been
mythologized as seidr.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.551
Their relationship with the land

00:08:30.635 --> 00:08:32.428
could have yielded a pantheon

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:35.514
of Vanir-like agriculture
and fertility deities.

00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:39.227
I say "might" and "could"
because unfortunately little

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.145
is known about this
region's history

00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:42.772
due to a lack of written records

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:46.525
and a climate that tends to
destroy archeological artifacts.

00:08:46.609 --> 00:08:48.277
Regardless of the myth's origin,

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:51.030
the war between the Aesir and
Vanir is a powerful reminder

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:53.241
that conflicts rooted
in anger and fear

00:08:53.324 --> 00:08:55.868
can still be resolved
through wisdom and mercy.

00:08:55.952 --> 00:08:58.496
In that spirit, we've
cooked up a fun treat for you

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:00.706
in this season of
"Fate and Fabled."

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.167
Dr. McT and I have
each picked five

00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:05.544
of our favorite
figures from mythology.

00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:07.338
It's kind of like
a fantasy football draft,

00:09:07.421 --> 00:09:09.382
but without
all the toxic competition.

00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:10.967
We'll reveal one of our choices

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.010
in each thematically
appropriate episode,

00:09:13.094 --> 00:09:14.637
and at the end of the season,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.598
we'll unite our pantheons
just like the Norse did.

00:09:17.682 --> 00:09:20.601
So to start us off, Dr. McT,
who's your first pick?

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:22.520
Oh, I'm so excited
for you to hear this.

00:09:22.603 --> 00:09:24.814
I am choosing Idunn.

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:26.732
-Do you know Idunn?
-Ooh, no.

00:09:26.816 --> 00:09:29.777
Idunn is an Aesir, she's
a goddess of fertility

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.988
and spring and rejuvenation,

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:35.116
but she's in charge of
planting the golden apples

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:39.245
that the Aesir used to stay
immortal and beautiful.

00:09:39.328 --> 00:09:40.496
That sounds like
something I want.

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:42.164
So I definitely
approve of this pick.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.459
Thank you! I do like the
option of living forever,

00:09:45.543 --> 00:09:47.295
so I wanted to give the people

00:09:47.378 --> 00:09:49.338
in our little utopia
that option.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:50.923
And the more gold
the better, in my book.

00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:51.924
Exactly.

00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:54.051
[ominous music]

00:09:54.135 --> 00:09:56.137
Excellent first pick
to start us off.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.139
I'll be making my first
pick of the pantheon

00:09:58.222 --> 00:10:00.016
at the end of the next episode,

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:02.852
but make sure you stay tuned
for every episode this season.

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.938
We'll reveal our pantheon
picks at the end of each.

00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:07.606
But maybe you'll remember
that better in verse.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.608
Is there any of that
poetry mead left?

00:10:09.692 --> 00:10:12.320
-Yes, there you go.
-Thank you.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.410
(Emily)
Ten gods chosen, five apiece,
from the world around.

00:10:19.493 --> 00:10:21.495
(Moiya)
In sky or sea
or deep dark pit

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:22.913
could they all be found.

00:10:22.997 --> 00:10:24.332
(Emily)
We'll share the tales
of people

00:10:24.415 --> 00:10:25.791
whose lives our choices touched

00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:27.376
and set aside the differences

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.086
that once they may have clutch.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.379
So stick around this season.

00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:32.131
We promise you won't yawn

00:10:32.214 --> 00:10:35.259
once you see who we draft
in our fantasy pantheon.

00:10:37.261 --> 00:10:38.637
Hey foodies, you're missing out

00:10:38.721 --> 00:10:40.056
if you're not watching
the new stuff cooking

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:41.682
over on PBS Food.

00:10:41.766 --> 00:10:44.226
Go on a tasty journey to find
the best South Asian food

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.228
in America on "Spice Road"

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:48.314
or get ready to swap
delicious recipes

00:10:48.397 --> 00:10:50.566
from different
cultures on "Pan Pals."

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:52.443
The channel has shows
covering the history

00:10:52.526 --> 00:10:54.820
of iconic dishes
to food science.

00:10:54.904 --> 00:10:56.906
Hit the link in our
description to check them out.

00:10:56.989 --> 00:10:59.533
Just don't watch these
on an empty stomach.

00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.660
I would wear this outfit though.

00:11:01.744 --> 00:11:03.245
I low-key would actually
probably wear this.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:04.497
-Yeah.
-Wait, wait, wait.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.249
Why not to the
Vaesir and the Anir?

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.292
That's not what they're called.

00:11:08.376 --> 00:11:09.293
Uh-oh.

